    "narrative": "The **Austin Waves** enter today\u2019s slate with a significant offensive focus on capitalizing against favorable matchups, headlined by **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88). Facing Littell, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from an elite combination of park factors and a strong 29 PA history, making him our primary engine for both power and counting stats. **Josh Lowe** (71.68) also provides an intriguing profile; while his batting order spot at #8 is suppressed, his elite sprint speed remains critical for our team\u2019s scarcity strategy in stolen bases, and he is well-positioned to exploit Civale\u2019s 4.77 xERA. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (69.73) and **Kyle Tucker** (67.83) are strong starts, with the former leaning heavily into a +14% dynamic platoon boost that overrides his concern regarding Bradish\u2019s arm.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involves **Coby Mayo** (60.58), who fell just shy of cracking the starting nine despite a highly favorable park environment and a targetable matchup against Littell. The optimizer ultimately favored the efficiency and batting order stability of players like **Drake Baldwin** and **Nolan Schanuel** to maximize our daily cap usage. While **Coby Mayo** remains a high-upside asset, his projected lower floor compared to our starters makes him the odd man out. Investors should monitor the weather for any late-breaking shifts, but for now, the primary risk remains the +5% wind-out factor potentially over-inflating expectations for fly-ball hitters like **Jackson Merrill** (58.91), who faces the toughest SP test of the day in Sheehan. We will continue to leverage our speed-heavy depth, including **Josh Lowe** and **Sam Antonacci**, to stay ahead in the stolen base category throughout the weekend.",
